  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: All four completed experiments confirm that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the strongest architecture (best: config_041, acc=0.725, F1=0.685). The only major design axis not yet explored within this optimal architecture is the RNA encoder—scvi_n200 has been used in every experiment, while scgpt (a more expressive generative single-cell model) remains untested in this setting. Question: Does replacing scvi_n200 with scgpt, while keeping imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile fixed, yield a further accuracy gain? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly exploits the strongest known architecture and tests the single most impactful untested variable (RNA encoder quality). scgpt's richer learned representation plausibly captures cell-state information that scvi_n200 misses, making it the highest-expected-value exploration. If it improves, we have a new best; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can pivot to image-encoder variations. Expected relative cost: scgpt is a larger generative model than scvi_n200, so I estimate ~4.5–5.5 GPU hours—moderately higher than config_041 (3.60) but comparable to config_025 (4.65). This is justified given the potential accuracy upside and the 5 remaining experiments."
}

